            <div xml:id="d267">

                <pb facs="0254" n="242" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg242"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">891.01A/176: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Minister in Iran</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Dreyfus</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-06-27T18:00:00-04:00">June 27, 1942—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>167. Your 316, June 26. Please tell Prime Minister that delay in furnishing
                    advisers has in no way been due to lack of interest on part of this Government.
                    On contrary, Department has been and is continuing to make every effort to
                    locate suitable men. We fully appreciate importance of this question and hope to
                    achieve concrete results in near future. Prime Minister will understand that
                    demands of our own war effort make it doubly difficult to secure services of men
                    with high qualifications needed for such positions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
